# Keeps `docker compose build`'s context small -- everything here gets
# excluded from what's sent to the Docker daemon before the build even
# starts. This matters independently of layer caching: a huge context
# gets re-uploaded on every single build regardless of cache hits, which
# is its own source of slowness separate from whether pip reinstalls
# anything. node_modules/ is almost certainly the single biggest
# contributor here -- the whole point of this file is that the backend
# image (build: . -> COPY backend/ ./backend/) never touches any of the
# frontend at all.

.git
.gitignore

# Frontend -- entirely unrelated to the backend image
node_modules
src
public
index.html
package.json
package-lock.json
vite.config.js

# Repo-level docs -- irrelevant to the build, no reason to upload them
README.md
LICENSE

# Model data -- Vosk is bind-mounted as a volume at runtime, Kokoro is
# fetched by its own explicit RUN step in the Dockerfile. Neither should
# ever be pulled in via COPY/build context.
models/
knowledge_base/

# Python/OS cruft -- stale .pyc files from running things locally (e.g.
# backend/__pycache__) shouldn't ride along into the image either
__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
venv
*.egg-info

# Editor/OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
